From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc_vpu: allow the T10/T20 NVPU register window for IOCTL_CHANNEL_WOR_VPU_REG

On top of 0102.  0102 limits IOCTL_CHANNEL_WOR_VPU_REG to the Helix /
Radix (/ T23 IVDC) windows.  A T10/T20 kernel (CONFIG_JZ_NVPU) defines
none of them, so every read returns -EPERM there.  The stock T20 libimp
3.12.0 rate control (and OpenIMP's port, src/rc_t20) reads the motion
statistics 0x132800e4/e8/ec after every picture through this ioctl;
with -EPERM they read as 0 and the rate control misjudges the scene.

Allow aligned words inside the jz-vpu platform window VPU_IOBASE(i) +
1 MiB (0x13200000..0x132fffff on T10/T20; CONFIG_VPU_NODE_NUM units),
the same window the NVPU driver itself maps.

---
 drivers/video/soc_vpu/soc_vpu.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/soc_vpu/soc_vpu.c b/drivers/video/soc_vpu/soc_vpu.c
index 74d236f2..3a0e36de 100644
--- a/drivers/video/soc_vpu/soc_vpu.c
+++ b/drivers/video/soc_vpu/soc_vpu.c
@@ -1119,6 +1119,24 @@ static bool soc_vpu_reg_allowed(unsigned int paddr)
 	if ((paddr >= RADIX_IOBASE) && (paddr < RADIX_IOBASE + SOC_VPU_REG_WINDOW))
 		return true;
 #endif
+#if defined(CONFIG_JZ_NVPU) && defined(VPU_IOBASE)
+	/*
+	 * T10/T20 NVPU: the jz-vpu platform window VPU_IOBASE(i) + 1 MiB.  The
+	 * stock T20 libimp rate control reads 0x132800e4/e8/ec there after
+	 * every picture (i264e_ratecontrol_priv_init/_end).
+	 */
+	{
+#if defined(CONFIG_VPU_NODE_NUM)
+		int n = CONFIG_VPU_NODE_NUM;
+#else
+		int n = 1;
+#endif
+		for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+			if ((paddr >= VPU_IOBASE(i)) && (paddr < VPU_IOBASE(i) + SOC_VPU_REG_WINDOW))
+				return true;
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 #if defined(CONFIG_SOC_T23) && defined(IVDC_IOBASE)
 	/* IVDC (direct ISP->VPU path), as mapped by the Helix driver */
 	if ((paddr >= IVDC_IOBASE) && (paddr < IVDC_IOBASE + 0x1000))
